    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Spiral" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="36.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Point B is placed by a rule: its distance from the center is A's x-coordinate and its angle is A's y-coordinate. As A slides along the segment, B sweeps out a spiral.\n\nThe curve is drawn through 60 points, so only the height of the segment matters: it sets how far the angle turns from one point to the next. A turn of 90° makes squares, 120° triangles, 72° pentagons and 60° hexagons — drag the top end onto an orange ring and see." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="84.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
